Dear,

After centering and scaling of the covariates, I have an error in the code I can't solve. This is the code:

N70 = nrow(strandline70)
X70 = data.frame(Intercept = rep(1, N70),
                 sanddynamics = strandline70$dyn_converted,
                 springtide = strandline70$spr_converted)
StackFit = inla.stack(tag = "Fit",
                          data = list(y = strandline70$Abundance_median),
                          A = list(A3, 1),
                          effects = list(w3.index, X70))
FIT = inla.stack(StackFit)

sanddynamics = as.matrix(strandline70$dyn_converted)
springtide = as.matrix(strandline70$spr_converted)

f0 = y ~ -1 + Intercept + poly(springtide, 2) + poly(sanddynamics, 2)
inla0 = inla(f0,
            family = "zeroinflatedpoisson0",
            control.compute = list(waic = TRUE),
            data = inla.stack.data(StackFit),
            control.predictor = list(A = inla.stack.A(StackFit)))

The error:

*** inla.core.safe:  The inla program failed, but will rerun in case better initial values may help. try=1/1
Error in inla.core.safe(formula = formula, family = family, contrasts = contrasts,  :
  missing values are not allowed in 'poly'
The inla program failed and the maximum number of tries has been reached.

There are no NA's in the Stack. I have converted the covariates into matrixes for the poly() function to recognize them, but that didn't do the trick. Can someone please help?

Thanks in advance!

Kind regards,
Charlotte

