> > > >
> > > > Ap <- inla.spde.make.A(
> > > >     mesh = mesh,
> > > >     loc = cbind(pred.data$x, pred.data$y)
> > > > )
> > > >
> > > > fun2 <- function()
> > > >     return(
> > > >         iIntercept +
> > > >         x1 * pred.data$x1 +
> > > >         Ap %*% s
> > > >      )
> > > >
> > > > PS.: You can consider the inlabru package that facilitates working with SPDE models in INLA.
> > > >
> > > > best regards,
> > > > Elias
