MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I am running a lgcp to predict distribution of a particular species on an area that has been unevenly sampled.

I have a samplers object that consists of an sf dataframe with different polygons in different rows and a column called weight proportional to the number of times each polygon has been sampled.

I am using the fm_int function to calculate the integration points ahead of the modelling using

ips <- fm_int(mesh, samplers = samplers)

and then model using

lgcp(formula, data, ips)

1/ am I correct in assuming that the weights column in the samplers argument can be used to account for uneven sampling?

2/ Should the weights I provide be directly or indirectly proportional to the sampling effort?

