On Mon, 2024-05-13 at 05:24 -0700, Yessika Adelwin Natalia wrote:
> Dear INLA community
>
> I have a spatiotemporal joint Binomial-Poisson model with this definition:
> r_ijk  ~ Binomial (n_ijk, p_ijk )
> logit⁡(p_ijk)= β_01 + β_1k1 + β_21[immune]_ijk + γ_k1*[immune]_ijk
> +  ν_(i1) + γ_(j1) + δ(ij1)
>
> O_ij  ~ Poisson (N_ij,IR_ij )
> log⁡(IR_ij)= β_02+  β_1k2   + β_22 [immune]_ijk   + γ_k2*[immune]_ijk
> + ν_(i2) + γ_(j2) + δ(ij1)
>
> with  i = areal unit (1,...,93), j = temporal unit (1,...,16), k = age groups
> (1,...,8), ν_(i1) & ν_(i2) spatial structured random effect, γ_(j1) & γ_(j2)
> temporal structured random effect, δ_(ij1) & δ_(ij2) spatiotemporal
> interaction. The data are structured for a joint model fit (in a list with Y
> as a matrix) with the following model formula:
>
