Subject: Error with INLA : Condition `nfactors >= nfac_from && nfactors <= nfac_to' is not TRUE
Message-ID: <VqhUKbu-QFo.cdJVtfSHAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/VqhUKbu-QFo/m/cdJVtfSHAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,
I am running a nonstationary INLA model, with varying kappa. I ran the model on my laptop with only three columns in B.kappa and B.tau in order to test whether it worked, and I had no trouble.  But I tried to run the model with full B matrices and I got a crash saying Error with INLA : Condition `nfactors >= nfac_from && nfactors <= nfac_to' is not TRUE. I have run models with nonstationary kappa on the same cluster before without trouble. Does this message seem familiar to you ?
Thanks to you all, as ususal
Sébastien

From u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com  Thu May 23 18:10:15 2024
From: u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com (Helpdesk [Haavard Rue])
Date: Thu, 23 May 2024 18:10:15 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Error with INLA : Condition `nfactors >= nfac_from && nfactors <= nfac_to' is not TRUE
Message-ID: <VqhUKbu-QFo.oIzJOFqMAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <VqhUKbu-QFo.cdJVtfSHAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <VqhUKbu-QFo.cdJVtfSHAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/VqhUKbu-QFo/m/oIzJOFqMAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

you have to many hyperparameters for the integration schemes that are
predefined. You have to construct your own (see vignette), or just use the
option

control.inla=list(int.strategy="eb")

maybe you want to add also force.diagonal=TRUE in that case, which I think would
be useful

