Dear Finn and all,

Thank you for your quick help response.  I followed the approach by adding  control.predictor = list(link = 1) to the inla() function call. But some of the summary.fitted.values are coming up as negative numbers. Is this something expected ? I thought all the summary.fitted.values were supposed to be positive numbers.

On Fri, 24 May 2024 at 11:53, Finn Lindgren <finn.l...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi,
> Use control.predictor = list(link = 1) to tell inla to apply the link function when computing the fitted.values output. Then they will already be on the probability scale.
> Finn
>
> > On 24 May 2024, at 10:33, Mcewen Khundi <mcewen...@gmail.com> wrote:
> >
> > ﻿Hello,
> >
> > I have the code below and would like to get advice.
