If you add covariates that are NA, then the will be converted to 0.0 if they are
continous and `empty' if its a factor.

 inla(y ~ x + fac, data=data.frame(y=c(0,0,0), x=c(1,2,NA),
fac=as.factor(c('a',NA, 'b'))))$model.matrix
"dsparseModelMatrix": 3 x 3 sparse Matrix of class "dgCMatrix"
  (Intercept) x facb
1           1 1    .
2           1 2    .
3           1 .    1
@ assign:  0 1 2
@ contrasts:
$fac
[1] "contr.treatment"

